<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amoghavarsha III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 936–939</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Baddega</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amoghavarsha III, also called Baddega, was Rashtrakuta emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> from about 936 to 939. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indra-iii">Indra III</a> and uncle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/govinda-iv">Govinda IV</a>, he was placed on the throne by nobles and feudatories, backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vemulawada">Vemulavada</a>, after Govinda IV's unpopular reign ended in revolt. A ruler of religious temperament, he left much of the government to his son and successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna-iii">Krishna III</a>.</p></div>
